# Flexibility in Decision-Making

Flexibility in decision-making emphasizes the importance of adapting decisions as new information emerges, since rigidity can lead to irrational choices based on outdated or irrelevant factors.

## Core Idea

Ariely emphasizes the importance of being flexible when making decisions, as rigidity can lead to irrational choices based on outdated or irrelevant factors.^[raw/articles/the-upside-of-irrationality---dan-ariely.md]

## Key Principles

- Decisions should be revisable as context changes
- Rigid commitment to past choices prevents optimal adaptation
- Flexibility requires awareness of one's own inertia and default patterns
- Re-evaluation is not the same as inconsistency

## Connection to Existing Concepts

This concept connects to [[real-options-analysis]] (treating decisions as flexible options) and [[strategic-vs-reactive-thinking]] (long-term orientation vs short-term rigidity).